    {
      "id": 196039,
      "name": "Sonvar",
      "username": "Powerhound_2000",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-04-16T23:53:11.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It used to be that his Traps were face up in the deck to start. &nbsp;When revealed they did their thing, got shuffled into the deck face up again, and then played the top card of the deck. &nbsp; It got changed to this:</p><ul>\n<li>At the start of the game, turn all Trap cards in Ambuscade’s deck face up.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Whenever a Trap card would be discarded, first the top card of the villain deck is played, then the Trap card is discarded.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Whenever the villain trash is shuffled into the villain deck, all Trap cards are turned face up.</li>\n</ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The reason was that if you prevented Ambuscade from dealing damage you could end up in an almost never ending loop of Traps being played.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:23:28.398Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 16534,
      "topic_slug": "villain-challenges",
      "display_username": "Sonvar",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
