      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": "",
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>It used to be that his Traps were face up in the deck to start. &nbsp;When revealed they did their thing, got shuffled into the deck face up again, and then played the top card of the deck. &nbsp; It got changed to this:</p><ul style=\"margin-top: 0.3em; margin-left: 1.6em; list-style-image: url(data:image/svg+xml,%3C%3Fxml%20version%3D%221.0%22%20encoding%3D%22UTF-8%22%3F%3E%0A%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20version%3D%221.1%22%20width%3D%225%22%20height%3D%2213%22%3E%0A%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%222.5%22%20cy%3D%229.5%22%20r%3D%222.5%22%20fill%3D%22%2300528c%22%2F%3E%0A%3C%2Fsvg%3E%0A); color: rgb(54, 43, 54); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1em;\">At the start of the game, turn all Trap cards in Ambuscade&rsquo;s deck face up.&nbsp;</li><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1em;\">Whenever a Trap card would be discarded, first the top card of the villain deck is played, then the Trap card is discarded.&nbsp;</li><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1em;\">Whenever the villain trash is shuffled into the villain deck, all Trap cards are turned face up.</li></ul><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1em;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0.1em;\">The reason was that if you prevented Ambuscade from dealing damage you could end up in an almost never ending loop of Traps being played.&nbsp;</p>",
