    {
      "id": 196040,
      "name": "Natediggadoggity",
      "username": "Natediggadoggity",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/f04885/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-04-17T09:39:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I see, I tried it on the app today, and it’s still a little too strong, because one “armed and dangerous” can start a chain reaction that reveals several traps in a row before getting a device, and stacks several extra card plays on top of each other.</p>\n<p>I don’t think face up traps should stack a card play, and then he might finally have an appropriate power curve.</p>\n<p>I don’t mind him chaining card plays, that’s his mechanic, and if he’s lucky enough to play a quick stim patch into a run and gun several times in a row, that’s fine. He just got lucky.</p>\n<p>It’s when I know there’s an additional +3 card plays to wade through, which can each trigger their own run of additional chained plays together that it just gets ridiculous and un-fun.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:23:28.462Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
