      "raw": "I see, I tried it on the app today, and it's still a little too strong, because one \"armed and dangerous\" can start a chain reaction that reveals several traps in a row before getting a device, and stacks several extra card plays on top of each other.\r\n\r\nI don't think face up traps should stack a card play, and then he might finally have an appropriate power curve.\r\n\r\nI don't mind him chaining card plays, that's his mechanic, and if he's lucky enough to play a quick stim patch into a run and gun several times in a row, that's fine. He just got lucky.\r\n\r\n It's when I know there's an additional +3 card plays to wade through, which can each trigger their own run of additional chained plays together that it just gets ridiculous and un-fun.",
